## 9. Alternatives considered

| Alternative | Why not chosen |
|---|---|
| Workers return averages | Wrong answer when groups differ in size |
| Split files equally between workers at the start | The slowest worker decides the total time (~1.7× slower in simulation) |
| One machine combines all partial results | Breaks the 5-file limit and becomes a bottleneck |
| Combine in fixed rounds (wait for each level) | Fast workers sit idle waiting for slow ones |
| Put all of a job's tasks on the queue at once | A large job blocks every job submitted after it |